    "result": "Explicit attention is wrong in exactly the heads whose first score element lies beyond 2^32 (2^32 / 9728^2 = 45.385: heads 46-55), identically in bf16 and fp16, and correct in every head at 8,704 rows, where the whole 56 x R^2 score tensor (4,242,538,496 elements) is below 2^32. Head 45, which straddles the boundary, is correct. A probable Core AI defect: a 32-bit per-head offset in its unfused attention path (matmul or softmax) for tensors over 2^32 elements. PyTorch's own bf16 explicit attention is 0.0045 relative L2 at 9,728 (independent review), so bf16 precision is not the cause."
